===Etymology===
From {{der|en|dum|tatelen}}, {{m|dum|tateren|t=to babble, chatter}} (modern {{cog|nl|tatelen}}, {{m|nl|tateren|t=to talk, chatter}}), originally {{glossary|imitative}}.<ref>{{R:Lexico}}</ref> The word is cognate with {{cog|stq|tätelje|t=to talk nonsense, babble}}, {{cog|gml|tāteren}}, {{m|gml|tadderen|t=to babble, chatter}} (whence modern {{cog|nds-de|tatern|t=to chatter}}), {{cog|nds|tateln}}, {{m|nds|täteln|t=to cackle, gabble}}.<ref>{{R:New English Dictionary|part of speech=sb|volume=IX|part=2|page=111|column=2}}</ref> Compare also {{cog|enm|dadel}}, {{m|enm|dadull|t=tattling, gossip}}, and its alteration [[twaddle]].

